@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+---
+id: task-001-implement-json-pointer-rfc-6901-resolvepointer
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) resolvePointer"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`,
+resolving a JSON Pointer string against a JSON document and returning the referenced value. It throws
+when the pointer is not syntactically valid, or when it does not resolve to a value in the document.
+This is the first of a few features that build on each other; later features will call this function.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Wrote `src/index.test.ts` first (red): happy-path cases (whole-document, object member, nested
+  member, array index, falsy values `false`/`null`/`0`, `~0`/`~1` unescaping, unescaped special
+  characters) and error-path cases (non-string pointer, pointer not starting with `/`, missing member,
+  out-of-bounds/malformed array index, `-` array index, traversal through a scalar, invalid escape
+  sequence). Confirmed all 15 tests failed before any implementation existed.
+- Implemented `resolvePointer` in `src/index.ts` per RFC 6901 section 3-4: splits the pointer on `/`,
+  validates each raw reference token's `~` escapes before unescaping (`~1` → `/` then `~0` → `~`, in
+  that order), and walks the document distinguishing array traversal (strict `0`/`[1-9][0-9]*` index
+  syntax, no `-`, bounds-checked) from object traversal (own-property check only). Ran the suite again:
+  all 15 tests pass (green).
+- Added `typescript` as a devDependency (tsconfig.json already declared strict/declaration/outDir
+  settings but no compiler was installed) and `typecheck`/`build` npm scripts. `tsc --noEmit` passes
+  with no errors under `strict`. Excluded `src/**/*.test.ts` from the tsconfig `include` set so the
+  library build doesn't try to emit test files; Node's native TypeScript stripping still runs them
+  directly via `node --test` (no test-specific type definitions needed).
+- Documented `resolvePointer` with a usage example in `README.md` and a doc comment on the exported
+  function.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm test` — 15/15 passing.
+- `npm run typecheck` — no errors.
